    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Wildsong, we dive into the dynamic, surreal worlds of two acclaimed makers that highlight the unique versatility of the NDT 1 dancers. Choreographer Jan Martens creates his first world premiere for us, full of stamina, rebellion, and bold, punk-infused compositions. We also revisit the much-loved and theatrical Horses (2024) by our associate choreographer Marcos Morau. This programme will premiere during Holland Dance Festival. The performances in Amare, The Hague are accompanied by live music from the Dutch Ballet Orchestra. Conductor: Matthew Rowe, harpsichord: Gośka Isphording Please note: This performance contains flickering light, bright flashes and changing (colour) patterns. This may trigger an epileptic seizure in sensitive individuals. Read more here. Read everything about the performance in the online programme book The performances in The Hague on February 4, 5 and 6 are part of Holland Dance Festival 2026. We are proud of the collaboration with Holland Dance Festival. Amare is a great cultural venue with a wonderful dance theatre, and with its residents Nederlands Dans Theater and Holland Dance Festival, the aim is to raise The Hague’s profile even more as the dance city of the Netherlands. February 4 until March 22, 2026 Amare, The Hague February 4 (premiere), 5, 6 February 25, 26, 27 Practical information about your visit to Amare Schouwburg Tilburg February 10 Theater Rotterdam February 13 &amp; 14 Internationaal Theater Amsterdam February 18, 19, 20, 21 &nbsp; Stadsschouwburg Utrecht March 3 &amp; 4 Parkstad Limburg Theaters Heerlen March 7 SPOT, Groningen March 11 Parktheater, Eindhoven March 18 Chassé Theater, Breda March 22 Dancers This performance is danced by NDT 1. See an overview of all NDT 1 dancers Intermissions This performance contains 1 intermission and lasts approximately 2 hours. Introduction talks NDT provides introduction talks prior to nearly all performances throughout the Netherlands. In half an hour you will be introduced to the company and dive into the world of contemporary dance and NDT's repertoire. You will find the time and location of the introductions in Amare in the information e-mail prior to your visit. Information about the introductions in other theatres can be found on the website of the theatre in question."
