  {
    "@id": "https://www.ndt.nl/en/agenda/zo-ohadnaharin/",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#locale": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "en_US"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#locale:alternate": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "nl_NL"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#type": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "article"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "ZŌ"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "Choreographer Ohad Naharin, an unparalleled voice in contemporary dance, is back at NDT. In ZŌ, performed by NDT 1 and set in our NDT Black Box, the boundaries between audience and dancers blur, creating an intimate experience like no other. For now all tickets are sold out. Join the waiting list and you’ll receive an email when new tickets become available.  Choreographer Ohad Naharin, an unparalleled voice in the world of contemporary dance, continues to reinvent himself time and again.  Naharin began working with NDT more than 30 years ago, resulting in the creation of the acclaimed Minus 16 (1999) for NDT 2, as well as performances of beloved works from his repertoire, including The Hole (2013), which NDT 1 performed in the NDT Blackbox in 2023, to sold-out audiences and rave reviews..  In June and July 2026, we continue our long-standing collaboration with Naharin and present his latest groundbreaking creation ZŌ (2025) in the NDT Blackbox.  For ZŌ, Naharin collaborated with DJ Tai Rona, and together they created an immersive dance and sound experience in an intimate space where there is no longer any distance between audience and dancer.  In ZŌ, the audience is fully immersed in Naharin’s world—filled with theatricality, multilingual singing, dynamics, and humanity.  ZŌ premiered last December with Batsheva Dance Company and can be seen exclusively in The Hague at NDT. The production will not tour the Netherlands. June 11 till July 4, 2026  Amare, The Hague June 11 (premiere) t/m July 4  Practical information about your visit Dancers This performance is danced by NDT 1.  See an overview of all NDT 1 dancers Intermissions This performance contains no intermissions and the duration is 60 minutes."
      }
    ],
